<title>ISRAEL: Israel's Q2 unemployment falls to 6.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Israel's Q2 unemployment falls to 6.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Central Bureau of Statistics issued the following indicator on Thursday:</p>
<p>		    Q2 1996	Q1 1996	   Q2 1995</p>
<p>UNEMPLOYMENT    6.4 pct	6.6 pct	   6.7 pct</p>
<p>(seasonally adjusted)</p>
<p>The number of unemployed was 139,100, down 1.0 percent from the previous quarter and down 1.6 percent from the same quarter last year. The number of employed was 2.019 million, an increase of 2.0 percent from the previous quarter and up 3.2 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The number of people in the civilian work force was 2.158 million.</p>
</text>
